sentences.text:
...Respondents
(By Sri Yogesh D. Naik, Aga For R.1 & R.2;
Sri B.P. Puttasiddaiah, Advocate For R.3;
R.4 & R.5 Are Served.)

Hence, the following:
ORDER (i) Petitioner is given liberty to make necessary representation along with all the necessary particulars to respondent no.3, within a period of four weeks from today showing that he is the sole owner of the property, which is the subject matter of the writ petition, which has been acquired by the State for the purpose of KIADB;
(ii) If respondent no.3 is satisfied with the representation made by the petitioner,
then in that event, they are at liberty to withdraw the amount deposited by way of general award and pass a consent award as contemplated under Section 29(2) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act;

